# ================================
# ROBINOS ENGINEERING GOVERNANCE
# ================================

You are working on RobinOS production infrastructure.

# CORE RULES

- NEVER rewrite unrelated files.
- NEVER redesign existing UI unless explicitly requested.
- NEVER remove animations, layouts, spacing, or premium styling without permission.
- NEVER refactor entire systems for small fixes.
- ONLY modify the minimum required code for the requested task.
- Preserve existing architecture patterns.
- Preserve all production functionality.
- Preserve existing routes and auth flows unless explicitly instructed.
- Do not introduce placeholder code.
- Do not introduce mock data unless requested.
- Do not create duplicate components.
- Do not silently rename files, routes, variables, or APIs.
- Never break existing Supabase integrations.
- Never change environment variable names unless requested.
- Never change database schema unless explicitly requested.

# UI SAFETY RULES

- Maintain premium cinematic RobinOS aesthetic.
- Preserve dark blue glassmorphism design system.
- Preserve responsive behavior.
- Preserve mobile layouts.
- Preserve Framer Motion animations.
- Do not replace premium UI with generic Tailwind blocks.
- Do not modify typography scale globally.
- Do not alter navbar/footer structure unless requested.

# AUTH RULES

- Preserve Google OAuth flow.
- Never modify auth callback routes unless requested.
- Never remove session handling logic.
- Preserve protected route guards.
- Preserve RBAC logic.
- Preserve admin authorization checks.

# BACKEND RULES

- Preserve Supabase architecture.
- Never delete SQL migrations.
- Never modify production migrations unless explicitly instructed.
- Never expose service role keys.
- Preserve RLS policies.
- Preserve affiliate tracking logic.
- Preserve subscription entitlement logic.

# ENGINEERING BEHAVIOR

- Think before editing.
- Analyze dependencies before modifying files.
- Prefer surgical fixes over rewrites.
- Explain what files are being modified before editing.
- Keep code production-grade and deterministic.
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions.
- Avoid overengineering.
- Avoid speculative changes.

# FILE MODIFICATION RULES

- Only touch files directly related to the task.
- Do not auto-format unrelated files.
- Do not reorder imports unnecessarily.
- Do not regenerate entire files for small edits.
- Preserve comments and developer notes.

# ROUTING RULES

- Preserve all existing routes.
- Never remove callback handlers.
- Never alter dashboard routing unintentionally.
- Ensure auth redirects remain stable.

# DEPLOYMENT SAFETY

- Ensure Vercel compatibility.
- Ensure production build stability.
- Ensure TypeScript compatibility.
- Ensure no hydration-breaking logic.

# BEFORE COMPLETING TASKS

Always verify:
1. Existing functionality still works
2. Auth flow still works
3. Routing still works
4. UI consistency remains intact
5. No unrelated files changed
6. No production regressions introduced

# Core Rules

- Never modify authentication flows without approval
- Never change database schema automatically
- Never execute destructive migrations
- Never remove existing business logic without explicit confirmation
- Preserve affiliate attribution lifecycle
- Preserve RLS compatibility
- Never replace architecture patterns globally
- Prefer minimal scoped changes
- Always analyze impact before editing
- Generate implementation plan before execution
- Never touch production credentials
- Never rewrite entire files unless necessary

- Never modify environment variable structure without approval
- Never disable existing security checks or validation
- Prefer extracting components over rewriting existing systems
- If uncertain about architectural intent, ask before implementing